title: Unanswered demands

# Pressure events.
#
# Every domain here pairs a demand the Left has put on the national agenda with
# the ledger that can answer it. When the demand stays unanswered long enough,
# the people behind it stop waiting for Parliament: nurses strike, tenants
# march, the Commission audits, an office collapses, a case dies. The event
# always costs whoever owns the office, and the responses either convert the
# grievance into Left ownership, spend real authority to answer it, or leave it
# to grow into somebody else's mobilisation.
#
# These carry a low priority on purpose. A dated historical event always
# outranks them; they fill the months when nothing scheduled is waiting.

@health_strike
# prose-audit: Grade A — The staffing dispute is named through OZZPiP, the NFZ tariff and a specific closed ward rather than a capacity score, and each response ends somewhere different: the union owning the grievance, the tariff actually rising, a mediated postponement that the organisers can read, or a decision to leave the picket to somebody else.
title: The wards stop waiting for the Sejm
subtitle: Unanswered health demands become a nurses' and paramedics' strike
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 18
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and formation_in_progress = 0 and health_pressure_unmet >= 22 and pressure_top_domain = "health" and health_pressure_event_timer <= 0 and pressure_event_cooldown <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.health_pressure_event_timer = 9;
Q.pressure_event_cooldown = 3;
Q.pressure_events_resolved += 1;
Q.pressure_last_event = "Health strike";
const leftExecutive = Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government;
Q.pressure_strike_owner = leftExecutive
    ? (String(Q.health_minister_party || "") == "Lewica"
        ? "Lewica's own ministry"
        : "the coalition")
    : String(Q.government_name || "the cabinet");
if (leftExecutive) {
    Q.government_delivery -= 3;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
    Q.labor_dissent += 3;
    Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.15;
} else {
    Q.government_delivery -= 4;
    Q.public_trust -= 2;
    Q.konf_poll_momentum += 0.12;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "Hospital wards close as the staffing dispute reaches the street";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The staffing dispute leaves the committee room

The Ogólnopolski Związek Zawodowy Pielęgniarek i Położnych has stopped
negotiating about the negotiation. Referral desks are covered by the statutory
minimum, elective surgery lists have been suspended in four voivodeship
hospitals, and the paramedics have joined with the demand nobody has answered
in three budget cycles: a tariff from the NFZ that pays for the staff a ward
actually needs.

[? if health_capacity < 45: They are not striking against a service that works.
Wards have been running below safe staffing for long enough that the union no
longer treats it as an emergency, and the demands read like a list of things
that were promised and then went quiet.?][? if health_capacity >= 45: The
service is not collapsing, which is what makes the dispute hard to dismiss and
hard to win: nothing is on fire, and the people who keep it that way have
decided they have asked politely for long enough.?]

Every one of those demands has our name on it. We are the party that put them
on the agenda, in three consecutive budget cycles, with our own speeches
quoted back at us from the picket.

The dispute belongs to **[+ pressure_strike_owner +]** in every newspaper this
week. What the strike becomes depends on whether anyone converts it into a
settlement, a political property, or a vacancy for somebody else.

- @health_back_strike
- @health_settlement
- @health_bill
- @health_mediate
- @health_stand_aside

@health_back_strike
title: Stand on the picket line and make the demand ours
subtitle: The union keeps the dispute; Lewica gains the credibility and, in government, the cabinet's anger.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pressure_last_response = "Backed the strike";
Q.health_policy_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.health_policy_pressure - 8);
Q.labor_credibility += 6;
Q.public_sector_support += 5;
Q.workers_support += 3;
Q.women_support += 2;
Q.issue_ownership += 3;
Q.labor_dissent -= 5;
Q.social_spending_salience += 3;
if (Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 8;
    Q.ko_relation -= 4;
    Q.government_delivery -= 2;
    Q.coalition_blur -= 4;
} else {
    Q.negotiation_capital += 2;
    Q.media_capacity += 2;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica joins the hospital picket and adopts the staffing demand";
!}

Our MPs spend the week where the dispute is, not where it is discussed. The
demand stops being a line in a party programme and becomes a number the union
and we defend together: staffing norms in the tariff, and the money to pay for
them.

[? if left_in_government: The cost arrives at the cabinet table on Tuesday. A
governing party on a picket line against its own coalition's budget is a
contradiction our partners are entitled to name, and they name it at
length — but nobody on the ward believes we abandoned them for a portfolio.?][?
if not left_in_government: The cabinet's answer is that the opposition is
importing conflict into the health service. The organisers, who have been
asking for three years, are not persuaded that it was imported.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Go to the picket

@health_settlement
title: Fund the staffing settlement through the ministry
subtitle: Cost: 2 budget capacity. The demand is answered rather than represented.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and budget >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: A funded settlement needs a functioning cabinet and two budget points.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pressure_last_response = "Funded a staffing settlement";
Q.budget -= 2;
Q.health_policy_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.health_policy_pressure - 22);
Q.health_capacity += 6;
Q.government_delivery += 5;
Q.labor_credibility += 4;
Q.public_sector_support += 4;
Q.fiscal_stress += 2;
Q.government_goal_health = 2;
Q.labor_dissent -= 6;
if (String(Q.government_party || "") == "pis") {
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
    Q.pis_relation -= 2;
} else {
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 4;
    Q.psl_coalition_dissent += 2;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The staffing tariff rises and the hospital strike ends in a settlement";
!}

The tariff is rewritten with staffing norms attached, backdated to the quarter
the dispute began, and the ministry publishes the ward-level numbers it will be
held to. The strike committee suspends the action the same evening.

The Finance Ministry records that this was not in the plan and will be in every
plan from now on. That is what answering a demand costs: the money leaves the
reserve, the obligation does not.

- @poland_event_queue: Fund the settlement

@health_bill
title: Table the costed staffing bill and force a recorded vote
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Opposition cannot fund a tariff; it can make refusing one expensive.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The caucus has no research capacity left this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pressure_last_response = "Tabled a costed staffing bill";
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.health_policy_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.health_policy_pressure - 6);
Q.labor_credibility += 3;
Q.public_sector_support += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.negotiation_capital += 3;
Q.issue_ownership += 2;
Q.government_delivery -= 2;
Q.last_policy_stage = "Proposal";
Q.last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition";
Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    "A costed staffing bill puts the hospital dispute on the Sejm record";
!}

The bill is short, fully costed and names the tariff line it changes. It will
not pass. Its purpose is that every deputy who votes against it does so beside
a published figure for what the wards need, in a week when the wards are on
television.

The government keeps the treasury and can leave our bill on the table
indefinitely. From today it has to leave it there in public.

- @poland_event_queue: Force the recorded vote

@health_mediate
title: Broker talks without a number
subtitle: Free. The dispute is postponed rather than settled, and the organisers can tell the difference.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pressure_last_response = "Brokered talks without money";
Q.health_policy_pressure = Math.max(0, Q.health_policy_pressure - 4);
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.labor_credibility -= 2;
Q.labor_dissent += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
Q.movement_autonomy -= 2;
if (Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.government_delivery += 1;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 2;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The hospital dispute is adjourned to another working group";
!}

We convene everyone, which is genuinely useful and costs nothing, and the
action is suspended for a working group with a reporting date. No tariff
changes.

The union's negotiators are professionals and read the communiqué carefully.
They notice that the number they asked for is not in it, and that the party
which promised to carry that number is now the party asking them to wait.

- @poland_event_queue: Broker the talks

@health_stand_aside
title: Leave the dispute to the unions and stay on other files
subtitle: No spend and no exposure; the vacancy on the picket line is filled by somebody.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pressure_last_response = "Stayed out of the dispute";
Q.health_policy_pressure += 4;
Q.labor_dissent += 5;
Q.labor_credibility -= 4;
Q.public_sector_support -= 3;
Q.far_right_agenda += 2;
Q.konf_poll_momentum += 0.12;
Q.turnout_readiness -= 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The left is absent from the hospital dispute it spent three years raising";
!}

We keep the parliamentary calendar and let the social partners resolve their
own dispute, which is constitutionally impeccable.

Konfederacja's regional organisers arrive at the hospital gate on Thursday with
coffee, a camera crew and a story about a state that pays for everything except
the people who do the work. They are wrong about the remedy and they are the
only party present.

- @poland_event_queue: Leave it to the unions

@household_protest
