= [+ date_label +] — The cost of living stops being a statistic

The march was called by tenants' associations in Warsaw, Wrocław and Gdańsk and
then, without anyone coordinating it, by residents' committees in a dozen
smaller cities. The demands are specific: an end to indexation clauses that
raise rent faster than wages, a heating tariff decision that does not arrive in
January, and a mortgage instalment that stopped being survivable two rate
decisions ago.

[? if household_security < 45: The squares are full of people who are not
activists. That is the part the political class keeps failing to absorb: this
is not a mobilised constituency, it is households that have run out of room and
have nowhere else to take it.?][? if household_security >= 45: Most of the
country is coping, which is exactly why the ones who are not have stopped
expecting sympathy and started expecting an answer.?]

The protest is aimed at **[+ pressure_protest_owner +]**.

Konfederacja's speakers are already booked for the smaller squares, where they
will explain that the state is the reason your rent went up. Somebody is going
to own this anger by Monday.

- @household_tenant_movement
- @household_shield
- @household_bill
- @household_summit
- @household_ignore

