    Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 2;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "A housing summit produces a communiqué and no indexation cap";
!}

Developers, municipalities, banks and two tenants' representatives sit in the
same room for six hours and produce a document everyone can sign because it
commits nobody.

The tenants' representatives leave early. Razem's organisers, who spent the
week stewarding a march, read the communiqué and ask which of the two documents
the party intends to be judged on.

- @poland_event_queue: Convene the summit

@household_ignore
title: Treat the march as somebody else's constituency
subtitle: No spend and no risk; the squares are addressed by whoever does turn up.
