Q.issue_ownership += 2;
Q.eu_institutional_trust += 2;
if (Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
    Q.government_delivery += 1;
} else {
    Q.negotiation_capital += 3;
    Q.government_delivery -= 2;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The recovery-fund beneficiary register is published milestone by milestone";
!}

Every milestone is listed with the office responsible, the reported completion
date and the actual state of the procedure. It is dull, checkable and
impossible to answer with an adjective.

[? if left_in_government: Two of the offices named are run by our coalition
partners, who learn about the publication from the press. The register is still
the reason the next payment request survives verification.?][? if not
left_in_government: The cabinet calls it a service to Brussels. The mayors
waiting on the delayed programmes call it the first document that told them
where their money went.?]

- @kpo_repair_delivery
- @poland_event_queue: Publish the register

@kpo_repair_delivery
title: Repair the milestones the ministry actually owns
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity. Only a cabinet can reopen a procedure and staff a monitoring committee.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and budget >= 1
