}
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica defends the recovery-fund file it spent two years questioning";
!}

Our MEPs argue that the delay is procedural, which is true, and that the
programme is sound, which is partly true.

The clarification requests do not go away, and the argument we spent two years
building — that this money should be audited by somebody who is not spending
it — has now been made by us in the opposite direction.

- @poland_event_queue: Defend the file

@kpo_let_it_run
title: Let the dispute run its course
subtitle: No spend; the delay compounds and the file keeps its owner.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pressure_last_response = "Let the audit run";
Q.kpo_scrutiny += 3;
Q.kpo_public_credit -= 2;
Q.eu_institutional_trust -= 2;
Q.government_delivery -= 2;
Q.konf_poll_momentum += 0.1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The recovery-fund delay compounds through another verification cycle";
!}

Nobody publishes anything and the file goes back to Brussels unchanged.

The next cycle takes another quarter. The programmes that were waiting are now
a year behind, in towns that were told the money was already theirs, and the
argument that Europe pays for nothing acquires another concrete example.

- @poland_event_queue: Let it run

