} else {
    Q.government_delivery -= 4;
    Q.public_trust -= 2;
}
Q.institutional_trust -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "A benefit register migration fails and the queues become the story";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The queue is the policy

The register migration was announced as modernisation and delivered as a
four-month backlog. Applications submitted in the old system cannot be found in
the new one, the helpline has a published waiting time of fifty minutes, and
three voivodeship offices have suspended new appointments entirely.

[? if administrative_capacity < 45: None of this is a scandal. It is a state
that has been asked to deliver more each year by people who have never once
funded the desk that does the delivering.?][? if administrative_capacity >= 45:
The system mostly works, which is why the failures are concentrated and
invisible — they happen to the people with the least capacity to complain about
them.?]

Every entitlement in the statute book is worth exactly as much as the office
that processes it.

- @admin_fund_offices
- @admin_publish_audit
- @admin_blame_ministry
- @admin_accept_backlog

