    !Q.caretaker_government;
if (leftExecutive) {
    Q.government_delivery -= 3;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
} else {
    Q.government_delivery -= 3;
    Q.public_trust -= 1;
}
Q.household_security -= 2;
Q.economic_issue_salience += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The heating season opens with higher bills and an unbuilt grid";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The heating season sends the invoice

The transition exists on paper. On the ground there are two unbuilt grid
connections holding up four hundred megawatts of onshore wind, a district
heating plant in a mid-sized city still burning coal because its replacement
was postponed twice, and a mining region whose retraining programme has a
budget line and no participants.

[? if climate_state_capacity < 45: There is a transition on paper and almost
no machinery to carry it: a plan, a target, a series of announcements, and
nobody employed to connect any of it to a building or a job.?][? if
climate_state_capacity >= 45: The machinery exists and moves too slowly for the
people standing in front of it, which is a better problem than having none and
sounds identical from a picket line.?]

The household that pays this month's bill did not choose any of it.

- @climate_public_programme
- @climate_just_transition
- @climate_publish_costs
- @climate_pass_it_on

