The bargain is signed with the regional union structures and the municipalities:
retraining with a wage floor during it, an employer of last resort for the
oldest cohorts, and a published timetable that does not move at every election.

It costs more than a slogan about green jobs and it is the only version of the
transition that the people carrying it have ever agreed to.

